{
  "_id": "isaiah1",
  "book": {
    "_id": "isaiah",
    "title": "Isaiah",
    "titleShort": "Isa.",
    "titleOfficial": "THE BOOK OF THE PROPHET",
    "subtitle": "",
    "summary": "",
    "chapterDelineation": "Chapter"
  },
  "chapter": {
    "bookTitle": "Isaiah",
    "delineation": "Chapter",
    "number": 1,
    "summary": "The people of Israel are apostate, rebellious, and corrupt; only a few remain faithful—The people’s sacrifices and feasts are rejected—They are called upon to repent and work righteousness—Zion will be redeemed in the day of restoration.",
    "chapterAugmentations": [],
    "verses": [
      {
        "text": "The vision of Isaiah the son of Amoz, which he saw concerning Judah and Jerusalem in the days of Uzziah, Jotham, Ahaz, and Hezekiah, kings of Judah.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 4,
            "end": 10,
            "text": "TG Vision."
          },
          {
            "start": 14,
            "end": 20,
            "text": "1 Ne. 19:23 (23–24); 3 Ne. 23:1."
          },
          {
            "start": 62,
            "end": 67,
            "text": "TG Israel, Judah, People of."
          },
          {
            "start": 97,
            "end": 103,
            "text": "2 Kgs. 15:13 (1–13); Hosea 1:1."
          },
          {
            "start": 105,
            "end": 111,
            "text": "2 Kgs. 15:30, 38 (13–38); Micah 1:1."
          },
          {
            "start": 113,
            "end": 117,
            "text": "2 Kgs. 16:20 (19–20)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 119,
            "end": 122
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Hear, O heavens, and give ear, O earth: for the Lord hath spoken, I have nourished and brought up children, and they have rebelled against me.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 4,
            "text": "Deut. 32:1; D&C 1:1 (1–2); 76:1."
          },
          {
            "start": 122,
            "end": 130,
            "text": "Deut. 32:19."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "The ox knoweth his owner, and the ass his master’s crib: but Israel doth not know, my people doth not consider.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 51,
            "end": 55,
            "text": "HEB stall or manger."
          },
          {
            "start": 77,
            "end": 81,
            "text": "TG Apostasy of Israel; God, Knowledge about; Ignorance."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 57,
            "end": 60
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Ah sinful nation, a people laden with iniquity, a seed of evildoers, children that are corrupters: they have forsaken the Lord, they have provoked the Holy One of Israel unto anger, they are gone away backward.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 3,
            "end": 9,
            "text": "TG Man, Natural, Not Spiritually Reborn."
          },
          {
            "start": 69,
            "end": 77,
            "text": "Isa. 57:4."
          },
          {
            "start": 87,
            "end": 97,
            "text": "D&C 38:11 (10–12)."
          },
          {
            "start": 175,
            "end": 180,
            "text": "TG Anger."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Why should ye be stricken any more? ye will revolt more and more: the whole head is sick, and the whole heart faint.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 17,
            "end": 25,
            "text": "HEB smitten."
          },
          {
            "start": 44,
            "end": 50,
            "text": "TG Rebellion."
          },
          {
            "start": 110,
            "end": 115,
            "text": "HEB diseased."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "From the sole of the foot even unto the head there is no soundness in it; but wounds, and bruises, and putrifying sores: they have not been closed, neither bound up, neither mollified with ointment.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 140,
            "end": 146,
            "text": "HEB squeezed out."
          },
          {
            "start": 174,
            "end": 183,
            "text": "HEB softened."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 45,
            "end": 53
          },
          {
            "start": 74,
            "end": 77
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Your country is desolate, your cities are burned with fire: your land, strangers devour it in your presence, and it is desolate, as overthrown by strangers.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 5,
            "end": 12,
            "text": "Deut. 28:51 (51–52)."
          },
          {
            "start": 16,
            "end": 24,
            "text": "Jer. 9:11; Micah 3:12; 2 Ne. 13:8."
          },
          {
            "start": 71,
            "end": 80,
            "text": "TG Israel, Scattering of."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 13,
            "end": 15
          },
          {
            "start": 38,
            "end": 41
          },
          {
            "start": 113,
            "end": 118
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "And the daughter of Zion is left as a cottage in a vineyard, as a lodge in a garden of cucumbers, as a besieged city.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 51,
            "end": 59,
            "text": "TG Vineyard of the Lord."
          },
          {
            "start": 64,
            "end": 65,
            "text": "IE a watchman’s hut."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Except the Lord of hosts had left unto us a very small remnant, we should have been as Sodom, and we should have been like unto Gomorrah.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 55,
            "end": 62,
            "text": "TG Israel, Remnant of."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 94,
            "end": 97
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Hear the word of the Lord, ye rulers of Sodom; give ear unto the law of our God, ye people of Gomorrah.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 40,
            "end": 45,
            "text": "Ezek. 16:46 (44–55)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "To what purpose is the multitude of your sacrifices unto me? saith the Lord: I am full of the burnt offerings of rams, and the fat of fed beasts; and I delight not in the blood of bullocks, or of lambs, or of he goats.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 41,
            "end": 51,
            "text": "TG Sacrifice."
          },
          {
            "start": 152,
            "end": 159,
            "text": "1 Sam. 15:22."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 16,
            "end": 18
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "When ye come to appear before me, who hath required this at your hand, to tread my courts?",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Bring no more vain oblations; incense is an abomination unto me; the new moons and sabbaths, the calling of assemblies, I cannot away with; it is iniquity, even the solemn meeting.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 14,
            "end": 18,
            "text": "TG Hypocrisy."
          },
          {
            "start": 19,
            "end": 28,
            "text": "1 Chr. 23:31 (28–32)."
          },
          {
            "start": 83,
            "end": 91,
            "text": "Lam. 2:6."
          },
          {
            "start": 108,
            "end": 118,
            "text": "Matt. 15:9."
          },
          {
            "start": 129,
            "end": 138,
            "text": "HEB endure. Ps. 101:5."
          },
          {
            "start": 146,
            "end": 154,
            "text": "Isa. 29:13."
          },
          {
            "start": 165,
            "end": 179,
            "text": "TG Solemn Assembly."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 140,
            "end": 145
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Your new moons and your appointed feasts my soul hateth: they are a trouble unto me; I am weary to bear them.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 9,
            "end": 14,
            "text": "Hosea 2:11."
          },
          {
            "start": 34,
            "end": 40,
            "text": "Amos 5:21."
          },
          {
            "start": 90,
            "end": 95,
            "text": "Isa. 43:24 (24–28)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 104,
            "end": 109
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "And when ye spread forth your hands, I will hide mine eyes from you: yea, when ye make many prayers, I will not hear: your hands are full of blood.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 92,
            "end": 99,
            "text": "1 Sam. 8:18; D&C 101:7 (7–8). TG God, Access to."
          },
          {
            "start": 141,
            "end": 146,
            "text": "HEB bloods; i.e., bloodshed. Isa. 59:2 (2–3)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Wash you, make you clean; put away the evil of your doings from before mine eyes; cease to do evil;",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 4,
            "text": "Jer. 7:3 (1–7). TG Baptism."
          },
          {
            "start": 19,
            "end": 24,
            "text": "TG Cleanliness; Purification; Purity."
          },
          {
            "start": 39,
            "end": 43,
            "text": "TG Evil."
          },
          {
            "start": 82,
            "end": 87,
            "text": "TG Repent."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Learn to do well; seek judgment, relieve the oppressed, judge the fatherless, plead for the widow.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 5,
            "text": "TG Learn."
          },
          {
            "start": 12,
            "end": 16,
            "text": "TG Good Works."
          },
          {
            "start": 23,
            "end": 31,
            "text": "HEB justice."
          },
          {
            "start": 33,
            "end": 40,
            "text": "TG Charity."
          },
          {
            "start": 56,
            "end": 76,
            "text": "IE give a just verdict to the fatherless."
          },
          {
            "start": 92,
            "end": 97,
            "text": "TG Widows."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Come now, and let us reason together, saith the Lord: though your sins be as scarlet, they shall be as white as snow; though they be red like crimson, they shall be as wool.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 21,
            "end": 27,
            "text": "D&C 50:10."
          },
          {
            "start": 66,
            "end": 70,
            "text": "TG Forgive; Sin."
          },
          {
            "start": 103,
            "end": 108,
            "text": "TG Purification."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "If ye be willing and obedient, ye shall eat the good of the land:",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 9,
            "end": 16,
            "text": "TG Teachable."
          },
          {
            "start": 21,
            "end": 29,
            "text": "TG Obedience."
          },
          {
            "start": 48,
            "end": 52,
            "text": "TG Abundant Life."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "But if ye refuse and rebel, ye shall be devoured with the sword: for the mouth of the Lord hath spoken it.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 21,
            "end": 26,
            "text": "TG Rebellion."
          },
          {
            "start": 40,
            "end": 48,
            "text": "TG Punish."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 103,
            "end": 106
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "How is the faithful city become an harlot! it was full of judgment; righteousness lodged in it; but now murderers.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 35,
            "end": 41,
            "text": "TG Apostasy of Israel."
          },
          {
            "start": 58,
            "end": 66,
            "text": "OR justice."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Thy silver is become dross, thy wine mixed with water:",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 21,
            "end": 26,
            "text": "TG Apostasy of Israel."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Thy princes are rebellious, and companions of thieves: every one loveth gifts, and followeth after rewards: they judge not the fatherless, neither doth the cause of the widow come unto them.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 4,
            "end": 11,
            "text": "TG Kings, Earthly."
          },
          {
            "start": 72,
            "end": 77,
            "text": "IE bribes. Ezek. 22:12. TG Bribe."
          },
          {
            "start": 113,
            "end": 122,
            "text": "HEB “do not do justice to.” TG Judgment."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 12,
            "end": 15
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Therefore saith the Lord, the Lord of hosts, the mighty One of Israel, Ah, I will ease me of mine adversaries, and avenge me of mine enemies:",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 98,
            "end": 109,
            "text": "D&C 101:58."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "And I will turn my hand upon thee, and purely purge away thy dross, and take away all thy tin:",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 11,
            "end": 28,
            "text": "HEB return; i.e., repeatedly chastise."
          },
          {
            "start": 46,
            "end": 51,
            "text": "Jer. 9:7; Mal. 3:3."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "And I will restore thy judges as at the first, and thy counsellors as at the beginning: afterward thou shalt be called, The city of righteousness, the faithful city.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 11,
            "end": 18,
            "text": "Jer. 33:7 (7–8)."
          },
          {
            "start": 55,
            "end": 66,
            "text": "TG Counselor."
          },
          {
            "start": 124,
            "end": 145,
            "text": "TG Jerusalem."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Zion shall be redeemed with judgment, and her converts with righteousness.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 4,
            "text": "TG Zion."
          },
          {
            "start": 28,
            "end": 36,
            "text": "HEB justice."
          },
          {
            "start": 46,
            "end": 54,
            "text": "TG Conversion."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "And the destruction of the transgressors and of the sinners shall be together, and they that forsake the Lord shall be consumed.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 60,
            "end": 68
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "For they shall be ashamed of the oaks which ye have desired, and ye shall be confounded for the gardens that ye have chosen.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 33,
            "end": 37,
            "text": "IE terebinth trees and gardens used in idol worship."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "For ye shall be as an oak whose leaf fadeth, and as a garden that hath no water.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "And the strong shall be as tow, and the maker of it as a spark, and they shall both burn together, and none shall quench them.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 24,
            "end": 30,
            "text": "IE as a tuft of inflammable fibers."
          },
          {
            "start": 84,
            "end": 88,
            "text": "Isa. 9:16 (16–21)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 121,
            "end": 126
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      }
    ]
  },
  "nextChapterId": "isaiah2",
  "prevChapterId": "songofsolomon8",
